// REJECTS: Unknown database type 'Frobnicate'
//
// `type:` takes any identifier as far as the grammar is concerned; the value is matched
// against the DatabaseType enum in the walker. The set is closed and it is large -- H2,
// Postgres, Snowflake, MemSQL, BigQuery, Databricks, Trino, Spanner and more all parse --
// which is exactly why a rewrite is tempted to keep the string and move on.
//
// Pinned because a permissive `type:` is invisible until execution: the connection loads,
// the model compiles, and the failure appears in whichever component tries to pick a SQL
// dialect. The message also distinguishes a genuinely unknown type from a vendor grammar
// extension missing off the classpath, which reports "Unsupported syntax" instead.
###Connection
RelationalDatabaseConnection fixture::neg::BogusType
{
   store: fixture::neg::Db;
   type: Frobnicate;
   specification: LocalH2 {  };
   auth: DefaultH2;
}
